 | ID | Removed code / behaviour | Last known revision | Why removed | Maintained replacement | Verification | Recovery path |
 |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
 | CLEAN-111 | Always-direct dialing for pool speed tests / IP health checks under `tun` network mode (no gateway fallback); batch speed test / IP health / retest-failed including the built-in 本地代理 row (hardcoded `http://127.0.0.1:7890`); gateway routing for a node whose host:port equals the local gateway itself | `v1.7.129` (`b589b76`) | With local Clash TUN active, direct dials are captured by TUN and routed per Clash rules — the node IP is usually unreachable from the Clash node's exit, so every imported node showed “timeout/unavailable”. The built-in 本地代理 row always timed out for Clash Verge Rev setups listening on 7897 instead of 7890, and batch “test all / retest failed / IP health” counted it as a failure, making the whole pool look dead. Routing the gateway node through the gateway itself self-looped / double-hopped. | `tun` mode now dials gateway-first (loopback gateway is not TUN-captured and matches the environment's real path) with direct fallback; the built-in 本地代理 row is refreshed to the discovered local gateway (7890/7897/7891/10808/10809) at load/save and at test time, excluded from batch speed test / IP health / retest-failed, and a node whose host:port equals the gateway is tested directly to avoid self-route; IP health reports the pool node's real exit IP instead of the Clash node's. | 6 new regression tests (tun gateway fallback with blocked direct, tun direct fallback without a gateway, direct mode never touching the gateway, tun IP health through the gateway tunnel, node==gateway detection, node==gateway testable in all modes); full Go suite, go vet, frontend `tsc --noEmit` and 30 packaging tests. | Inspect with `git show b589b76:backend/internal/proxy/speedtest.go` and `git show b589b76:backend/app.go`; restore tun-mode always-direct dialing only for historical comparison, never in place of the gateway-aware routing. |
+
+## v1.7.131 OAuth isolation and store-only Web Store CDP
+
+| ID | Removed code / behaviour | Last known revision | Why removed | Maintained replacement | Verification | Recovery path |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| CLEAN-112 | Browser-level `Target.setAutoAttach` on every page target plus `applyWebStoreCompatibilityToInitialTab` injecting UA override / `webstorePrivate` into startup `about:blank` / `chrome://newtab`; URL-sync `Page.navigate` of one-time OAuth/consent URLs and CDP click/key replay on those surfaces | `v1.7.130` (`52f629c`) | Auto-attach connected CDP to every new tab (blank, OAuth popups, dapps). That made environment open slow and is a nodriver/tampering signal. URL-sync then cloned `x.com/i/oauth2/authorize?state=…` onto every follower, consuming the one-time state and producing a storm of “You weren't able to give access to the App”. | `backend/navigation_guards.go` is the single owner: `shouldInjectWebStoreCompat` (store hosts only), `shouldMirrorSyncNavigation`, `shouldReplaySyncInput`. The watch uses `Target.setDiscoverTargets` and attaches only after a store URL is seen. Initial-tab inject skips blank/newtab. Sync records auth URLs as the baseline but never navigates or replays them. Profile/cookie/extension/wallet data is untouched. | New `navigation_guards_test.go` covers X/Discord/Google/GitHub OAuth vs GenLayer/X-home/Discord-channels; packaging guard forbids `Target.setAutoAttach` and requires store-URL gating; focused Go tests for the new predicates. | Inspect with `git show 52f629c:backend/webstore_compat_watch.go` and `git show 52f629c:backend/app_input_syncer.go`. Restore blanket auto-attach only for historical comparison, never in place of store-URL discover. |
